From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:44:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] Fix the value of BTN_LEFT

It is 0x110 per linux/input-event-codes.h, not 0x100; 0x100 is
BTN_0, a miscellaneous digitizer button no ordinary client cares
about. Clients match pointer buttons against the exact evdev code,
so every left click was silently ignored by foot - most visibly,
press-and-drag text selection never worked. Focus, window moving
and resizing all happen on the Cocoa side, which is why the broken
left button went unnoticed for so long (right and middle were
already correct).

Found with WAYLAND_DEBUG=1: wl_pointer.button carried 256.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6m1eevhAns3j85HMZYKna
---
 Sources/Seat/OwlPointer.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Sources/Seat/OwlPointer.h b/Sources/Seat/OwlPointer.h
index 5c836bb..dfea00c 100644
--- a/Sources/Seat/OwlPointer.h
+++ b/Sources/Seat/OwlPointer.h
@@ -21,9 +21,9 @@
 
 @class OwlSurface;
 
-// These come from linux/event.h
+// These come from linux/input-event-codes.h
 
-#define BTN_LEFT   0x100
+#define BTN_LEFT   0x110
 #define BTN_RIGHT  0x111
 #define BTN_MIDDLE 0x112
 
